  "notes": [
    "YTL (Zhejiang Yongtailong) 5300 / DTS353F three-phase meter, as sold by Elektramat and used by cFos. Registers of the manufacturer's register matrix.",
    "Addresses are the hex addresses of the matrix; function 03 reads them. The length column is in bytes: 4-byte values are IEEE 754 floats in two registers, 2-byte values one 16-bit register. The matrix gives no units; the units here are those used by cFos and Home Assistant users (V, A, Hz, kW, kvar, kVA, kWh, kvarh).",
    "Default: address 1, 9600 bit/s (1200, 2400 or 4800 optional), 8 data bits, even parity, 1 stop bit.",
    "Meter ID, baud rate, combined code, holiday/weekend tariff, cycle time, time and the tariff schedule are written with functions 06 or 16 (0x10).",
    "Not tested on a device."
  ],
